WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.315
Lesson 10.6.

00:00:02.315 --> 00:00:05.800
Restaking and points: pricing speculative yield.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.008
By the end of this lesson, you'll be

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:11.230
able to value restaking and points programmes without

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:13.855
letting unknown rewards drive position size.

00:00:15.155 --> 00:00:16.445
Here's the plan.

00:00:16.445 --> 00:00:18.130
First, the key ideas.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:20.845
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:20.845 --> 00:00:22.370
Then, your checklist.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.532
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:25.832 --> 00:00:30.155
Restaking reuses staked assets to secure more services, paying

00:00:30.155 --> 00:00:33.998
extra rewards and often points: an off-chain score that

00:00:33.998 --> 00:00:36.357
may or may not become a token.

00:00:36.357 --> 00:00:39.340
The risk stack grows at each layer: staking

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:42.594
→ liquid restaking token → restaking protocol →

00:00:42.594 --> 00:00:46.012
each service it secures → slashing conditions.

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:49.477
Professional rules: First, Plan with points at zero.

00:00:49.477 --> 00:00:52.012
Base the decision on yield you can measure.

00:00:52.012 --> 00:00:55.387
Next, Treat points as an airdrop bet:

00:00:55.387 --> 00:00:58.441
EV = P(payout) × value − costs.

00:00:58.441 --> 00:01:01.567
Then, Hedge price if you only want the yield:

00:01:01.567 --> 00:01:05.643
short the underlying perp (strategy #24), knowing the hedge

00:01:05.643 --> 00:01:09.001
doesn't cover a depeg of the restaking token.

00:01:09.001 --> 00:01:12.424
And finally, Cap it: speculative bucket

00:01:12.424 --> 00:01:15.076
only (≤ 5–10% of DeFi capital).

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:18.891
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:01:18.891 --> 00:01:22.842
$20,000 in a liquid restaking token:

00:01:22.842 --> 00:01:26.666
base staking yield ~3% ($600/yr).

00:01:26.666 --> 00:01:30.494
Points: you estimate a 30% chance of a

00:01:30.494 --> 00:01:34.911
payout worth $1,500, costing $200 in gas and

00:01:34.911 --> 00:01:38.646
bridging: the calculator → EV $250.

00:01:38.646 --> 00:01:42.074
Worth doing only if the position still makes sense

00:01:42.074 --> 00:01:45.031
at $600/yr and the risk stack is acceptable.

00:01:46.331 --> 00:01:48.991
Slashing, depeg of the restaking token, and

00:01:48.991 --> 00:01:51.711
the chance that points never become anything.

00:01:53.011 --> 00:01:54.471
Here's your checklist.

00:01:54.471 --> 00:01:56.006
Do it now, for real.

00:01:56.006 --> 00:01:59.461
First, Decision still works with points valued at zero.

00:01:59.461 --> 00:02:02.456
Next, Full risk stack written, layer by layer.

00:02:02.456 --> 00:02:05.351
Then, Sized inside the speculative bucket.

00:02:05.351 --> 00:02:08.096
And finally, Hedge (if any) and its gap understood.

00:02:09.396 --> 00:02:10.606
Question 1.

00:02:10.606 --> 00:02:12.151
Why value points at zero?

00:02:16.571 --> 00:02:19.977
The answer: They're not guaranteed to become anything, so

00:02:19.977 --> 00:02:22.561
a decision that needs them is a speculation.

00:02:23.861 --> 00:02:25.106
Question 2.

00:02:25.106 --> 00:02:27.241
What does a perp hedge on the underlying miss?

00:02:31.661 --> 00:02:35.221
The answer: The restaking token depegging from the underlying.

00:02:36.521 --> 00:02:37.791
Question 3.

00:02:37.791 --> 00:02:40.296
Name three layers of the restaking risk stack.

00:02:44.596 --> 00:02:49.442
The answer: Any three: staking/validators, the liquid restaking token,

00:02:49.442 --> 00:02:53.946
the restaking protocol, each service secured, slashing conditions.

00:02:55.247 --> 00:02:56.492
Let's recap.

00:02:56.492 --> 00:02:58.541
Plan with points at zero: Base the

00:02:58.541 --> 00:03:00.832
decision on yield you can measure.

00:03:00.832 --> 00:03:04.018
Treat points as an airdrop bet: EV

00:03:04.018 --> 00:03:06.866
= P(payout) × value − costs.

00:03:06.866 --> 00:03:09.331
Hedge price if you only want the yield.

00:03:09.331 --> 00:03:12.139
Cap it: speculative bucket only

00:03:12.139 --> 00:03:14.421
(≤ 5–10% of DeFi capital).

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:18.235
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:18.235 --> 00:03:20.230
Next up, Lesson 10.7: Being

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:23.222
the house: perp-exchange liquidity vaults.
